# CODEOWNERS — required review for privileged CI configuration (Issue #208)
#
# The governance rationale is documented authoritatively in SECURITY.md,
# "Review governance (CODEOWNERS + branch protection)": why the privileged CI
# paths need a designated owner, why owners are named as concrete org members
# (repo admins) rather than a non-existent team, and how these rules take
# effect once the default branch (Develop) enables "Require review from Code
# Owners" — codified as settings-as-code in .github/rulesets/develop.json
# (require_code_owner_review: true), which a repo admin applies. See also
# docs/archive/pr-summaries/pr-summary-208.md for the branch-protection steps.

# Privileged CI: workflows and any composite/local actions.
/.github/workflows/   @Green-Beret @nleck
/.github/actions/     @Green-Beret @nleck

# The settings-as-code branch-protection ruleset (the controls themselves).
/.github/rulesets/    @Green-Beret @nleck

# Protect this ownership map itself from unreviewed edits.
/.github/CODEOWNERS    @Green-Beret @nleck
